### Code Quality & Logic
**Risk:** If a trigger in `schema.sql` uses alternative formatting or spacing (e.g. `END ;` or lower-case), `schema.toUpperCase().indexOf('END;', m.index!)` returns `-1`. Adding 4 yields `3`, resulting in an invalid `slice` range that silently truncates the trigger body analysis instead of throwing an explicit error.

**Suggested Fix:**
```typescript
            const end = schema.toUpperCase().indexOf('END;', m.index!);
            if (end === -1) throw new Error(`Could not find 'END;' for TRIGGER ${name} in schema.sql`);
            body = schema.slice(m.index!, end + 4);
```
